<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices steady, firm undertone.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices steady, firm undertone.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices on Tuesday were steady on firm undertone and with arrivals at around 1,200 tonnes, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices also remained steady in thin trading as demand was poor. Business volume was dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices remained bearish as export and local demand was limited. Soymeal yellow was $320-321 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was $120-121 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export at west coast Indian ports and was 4,150 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on rail) condition. Business volume was dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
